# Functions currently over the size limit, frozen at their present length. Shell AND
# Python -- 15 of the rows below are *.py. Scope is verify_code_size.py's; the
# file-size.allow header states it.
#
# Format: <path> | <function> | <lines> | <reason>
#
# The gate refuses growth, new offenders, AND a stale entry — shrinking a function
# means updating its number here, deleting it once it drops under the limit. That
# is what stops the baseline becoming cover for the next one.
#
# Length is weak evidence on its own; this list is a queue, not an accusation.
# The refactor entries live in docs/refactoring-backlog.md F1/F2.
docs/scripts/generate_sbom.py | build_document | 86 | 88 -> 86 on 2026-09-30: comment sweep. PRIOR: F1 2026-09-04 reviewed, seam named: 80 code lines building SPDX packages and relationships from one triple-nested walk over the deps metadata. The seam is per-entry, _sbom_package(entry, versions), leaving build_document as the walk. Low risk and compare_sbom.py exists, but no in-repo suite asserts the document shape, so pair the split with one
linux/scripts/01-core/cross-meson.sh | ensure_meson_cross_file | 82 | 93 -> 82 on 2026-09-30: comment sweep. PRIOR: F1 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: 56 lines of shell computing substitutions plus a 37-line `cat > <ini>` heredoc that IS the Meson cross file (6 sections). The emitted half is a document, not a function; splitting the computation off leaves a wrapper around a template
linux/scripts/01-core/python_uv.sh | uv_sync_project | 89 | 111 -> 89 on 2026-09-30: comment sweep. PRIOR: 109 -> 111 on 2026-09-23: the sync's own status is returned before the chain ORT reconcile runs (` |  | return`), and the unpinned branch names the environment uv used so the reconcile targets it; the reconcile itself is uv_reconcile_chain_ort. PRIOR: F1 2026-09-04 reviewed, SPLIT WANTED, blocked on coverage not shape: 72 code lines, and the extras selection (UV_SYNC_EXTRAS vs --all-extras plus _uv_extras_to_exclude, ~22 lines) is a clean seam -> _uv_sync_extra_args. Nothing in linux/scripts/tests exercises uv_sync_project, so the split would be unverifiable, and the other half is the venv pin that stopped `uv sync` writing into root-owned /opt/venv
linux/scripts/02-toolchain/setup-dependencies.sh | main | 95 | 98 -> 95 on 2026-09-30: comment sweep. PRIOR: F1 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: 87 code lines that are a 5-valued-flag parse loop (plus -h and a catch-all) and an 11-command dispatch case, each arm 2-8 lines of source_module and install calls. Splitting yields eleven one-call wrappers and hides the lazy-sourcing pattern (TG1) the arms exist to show side by side
linux/scripts/03-media/build/gstreamer/common/setup-gstreamer.sh | _gst_xpy_write_config | 84 | F1 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: 14 lines of shell around a 70-line HOST_PYTHON heredoc that writes the meson python build-config JSON. The size is a Python payload (linted via extract_embedded_python.py), not shell control flow, so splitting the shell moves 14 lines. Same class as smoke-torch-venv.sh assert_pinned_versions
linux/scripts/05-frameworks/tvm-config.sh | append_tvm_cmake_args | 85 | 86 -> 85 on 2026-09-30: comment sweep. PRIOR: F1 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP, this is the ARG-table case: 71 code lines are 17 locals, a 15-option case, and the required-option sweep that makes a dropped option fail HERE instead of as a wrong -D hours into the compile. Every emit is already delegated to _tvm_emit_cross_args, _tvm_emit_llvm_args, _tvm_emit_compiler_cache_args and _tvm_emit_vulkan_args, and tests/test-tvm-cmake-args.sh covers it
linux/scripts/06-packaging/smoke-torch-venv.sh | assert_app_venv_parity | 91 | 92 -> 91 on 2026-09-30: comment sweep. PRIOR: F1 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: 20 lines of shell around a 72-line PY heredoc, and those 20 are the skip guard, the run, and the rc-to-pass/fail mapping. Splitting the wrapper moves 20 lines and leaves the number where it is
linux/scripts/06-packaging/smoke-torch-venv.sh | assert_pinned_versions | 355 | 356 -> 355 on 2026-09-30: comment sweep. PRIOR: F1 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP, top by size and worst by value: 44 lines of shell (resolve versions.env and uv.lock, export nine EXP_* vars, run, parse the TOLERATED count) around a 312-line embedded Python program, which is where KNOWN_DRIFT and the per-arch authority rules live. Splitting the wrapper cannot move this number and the payload is already linted through extract_embedded_python.py
linux/scripts/06-packaging/smoke-torch-venv.sh | main | 93 | 116 -> 93 on 2026-09-30: comment sweep. PRIOR: 115 -> 116 on 2026-09-26: the compute battery calls assert_tvm_codegen, which fails a TVM whose shipped compiler does not load (BACKLOG CON35). PRIOR: F1 2026-09-04 reviewed, seam named: the smoke's test plan, presence loop then numpy/torch ABI bridge then compute battery then the two asserts. The STV_COMPUTE battery, 50 lines including two PY heredocs and the ONNX-EP sentinel handling, is the extractable piece -> _stv_compute_battery. Left for a build window: 06-packaging, and that sentinel logic is what caught a permanently-green never-executed check

